# rclone Copy with -vv --dump headers

```bash
$ rclone version
rclone v1.65.0

$ rclone copy source:bucket/largefile.bin dest:bucket/largefile.bin -vv --dump headers

2024/06/15 12:00:00 DEBUG : rclone: Version "v1.65.0" starting with parameters [...]
2024/06/15 12:00:00 DEBUG : Creating backend with remote "source:bucket"
2024/06/15 12:00:00 DEBUG : Using config file from "/home/user/.config/rclone/rclone.conf"
2024/06/15 12:00:05 DEBUG : largefile.bin: Need to transfer - File not found at Destination
2024/06/15 12:00:05 DEBUG : largefile.bin: S3 bucket bucket path largefile.bin: Waiting for checks to finish
2024/06/15 12:00:05 DEBUG : largefile.bin: S3 bucket bucket path largefile.bin: Waiting for transfers to finish
2024/06/15 12:00:05 DEBUG : largefile.bin: MD5 = a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678abcdef01 from source
2024/06/15 12:00:10 DEBUG : largefile.bin: Copied (server-side copy)
2024/06/15 12:00:11 DEBUG : largefile.bin: MD5 = a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678abcdef01-3 from destination

2024/06/15 12:00:11 ERROR : largefile.bin: corrupted on transfer: md5 hash differ "a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678abcdef01" vs "a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678abcdef01-3"

2024/06/15 12:00:11 INFO  : largefile.bin: Removing failed copy

2024/06/15 12:00:11 ERROR : Attempt 1/3 failed with 1 errors and: corrupted on transfer: md5 hash differ
```

## Analysis Clues

- Source ETag: `a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678abcdef01` (32 hex chars, no suffix → single PUT ETag = MD5)
- Destination ETag: `a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678abcdef01-3` (32 hex chars + "-3" → multipart ETag)
- Server-side copy internally used multipart upload on the destination despite source being single-part
- rclone compares full-object MD5 with multipart ETag format → mismatch
- File size is identical (not a truncated upload)
- Not a network corruption issue — the transfer was server-side

